## User preferences

- when the initial answer listed only eight candidates, the user corrected: “前后端那么多东西，claude功能框架体系结构流程，乱七八糟的那么多，你就找了这几条过来糊弄我？” -> product parity work must begin with a system-domain map covering frontend, desktop shell, protocols, services, runtime, agent loop, models/context, tools/permissions, persistence, extensions, subagents, automation, workspace, artifacts, and integrations—not a menu-level feature list. [Task 1]
- when the user said “别施工，只回答问题就行” and asked to use a Luna high subagent -> keep this class of work read-only, preserve source/official references, categories, and unverified boundaries rather than modifying Atlas. [Task 1]
- when the user warned “你知识库都不是最新的” -> use current official documentation, record observation/version conditions, and do not turn stale product knowledge into a current Claude claim. [Task 1]

## Reusable knowledge

- Atlas’s execution chain in this source snapshot was `Composer/App.submit` → `useAtlasStore` → `BackendAdapter.startRun` → `/ws/chat` → `run_drive` → `AgentOrchestrator` → `run_phases` → `HermesRuntime.run_turn` → `AtlasKernel.run` → `complete_stream/ToolScheduler` → runtime events → renderer. `AtlasKernel` is the execution body; `HermesRuntime` is a compatibility facade and `core/atlas/agent/orchestrator.py` only re-exports `AgentOrchestrator`. [Task 1]
- Treat source entrypoints as static implementation evidence, not functional proof. In particular, `useAtlasStore` defaulted to `permission_mode: 'full_access'`, extension package code/prompts/themes could be metadata-only, and `resume`/`after_sequence` plus snapshots/interrupted-run paths require separate replay, persistence, restart, and side-effect-safety acceptance. [Task 1]
- The validated report covered 26 domains and 10 flows. Reopen its artifacts for detailed gap routing: `C:\Users\25011\.codex\visualizations\2026\10\20\01a15710-6e71-7663-946e-5c4448909a4a\atlas-claude-system-review\comparison.md`, `atlas-system-map.md`, `claude-system-map.md`, and `atlas-source-inventory.tsv`. [Task 1]
- Mechanical validation of 215 Atlas file/line references, links, table columns, and snapshot consistency proves report traceability only; it does not prove product runtime correctness. [Task 1]

## Failures and how to do differently

- the user asked for “最大化并行子代理”, isolated lanes, and “不要修改 Atlas 正式代码” -> allocate one worktree/branch per lane, keep writes in designated research evidence paths, and leave the dirty D:\\Atlas production tree untouched. [Task 1][Task 2]

## Reusable knowledge

- The continuation gate model is G0 exact artifact identity/SHA and version relation; G1 executable-code coverage; G2 UI↔IPC/RPC↔host/agent↔events/persistence chains; G3 agent-loop semantics; G4 a small real execution probe; G5 current Atlas `main` comparison; G6 machine-readable coverage/surface/end-to-end/backlog/finish-gate artifacts; G7 only after locally possible work is exhausted and residual unknowns have reproducible external causes. Required lane artifacts include `COVERAGE.md`, `SURFACE-MAP.tsv`, `END-TO-END-TRACES.md`, `ATLAS-IMPLEMENTATION-BACKLOG.md`, and `FINISH-GATES.md`, plus the core report set. [Task 2]
- Establish the actual repository root before reading taskbooks: the rollout cwd had only `outputs`/`work`; the gate document was recovered from `D:\\Atlas` Git history/object data at `origin/research/agent-reverse-dispatch-20261019`. Use bounded lane-specific PowerShell/Git commands if context-mode tooling is unavailable. [Task 2]
- Exact release identity comes from `manifest.json` and lane evidence, not a product name. Keep vendor archives/extraction trees outside Git; report hashes, package trees, short excerpts, paths, and original analysis rather than vendor archives or sensitive profiles. The Atlas baseline for the closeout was `main@aa6196f550098cc46081dc6db2c376cb87ddffa5`. [Task 1]
- Use the end-to-end evidence table shape: visible action/command → renderer/CLI entry → IPC/RPC method → host/agent handler → event/state write → persistence location → user-visible result → exact file/offset or runtime observation. Synthetic probes in isolated home/config scratch plus loopback providers can safely validate transport, queue, tool delegation, subagent linkage, restart persistence, and state transitions without claiming external model execution. [Task 2]
- For large Electron/ASAR packages, enumerate executable/script files first, then analyze entrypoints and chunks in bounded batches. Preserve file/byte/parse-failure/uncovered-module counts in `COVERAGE.md`; split by directory/chunk/entrypoint/module and use AST/local parsing after a heap timeout rather than retrying a monolithic bundle. [Task 2]
- Static package identity, help output, strings hits, a desktop window, restored historical metadata, and `thread/resume` are not proof of Agent execution, UI↔IPC completion, or resumed unfinished work. Capture a real operation plus event/log/result, and distinguish state restoration from continuation of model/tool/child execution. [Task 1][Task 2]

## Failures and how to do differently

